Derived source
--------------

`crates/mm-harvest/src/imphash_ordinals.rs` — the Winsock and OLE automation
ordinal-to-name tables are transcribed from pefile, so that this project's
`imphash` matches the value every other tool reports for the same file.

    pefile — Copyright (c) 2004-2023 Ero Carrera
    MIT licence, https://github.com/erocarrera/pefile

`crates/mm-raw/src/ghost.rs` and the `$LogFile` operation names follow the
code-to-operation mapping published by jschicht's LogFileParser; the numeric
codes are the shared invariant, not the labels.

Linked dependencies
-------------------

Everything that links into `malmathic.exe` is MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, Zlib,
Unlicense or CC0 — permissive, and compatible with the terms in LICENSE. The
full set is pinned in Cargo.lock and listed in
`crates/malmathic/tests/audited-dependencies.txt`.

One test-only dependency is not. `nt_hive2` (and the `marvin32` and
`memoverlay` crates it brings) is GPL-3.0. It is a `[dev-dependencies]` entry
of `mm-harvest`, kept as an independent second registry-hive implementation to
differential-test this project's own readers against; no part of it reaches the
shipped binary. A test binary built from this tree does link it, so a test
binary is not yours to redistribute under the terms in LICENSE.
